config BR2_PACKAGE_FALCON_MKSTICK32
	bool "falcon-mkstick32"
	help
	  falcon-boot's mkstick, built static for a 32-bit machine:
	  installs, checks and removes falcon station-legacy on a disk
	  (`station install --bios --legacy`), so a machine that cannot
	  boot a 64-bit Linux can have the station put on its own disk
	  from DevLink recovery. The station's files come from the disk
	  or card it runs from, not from this binary.

	  https://git.airies.net/vifair22/falcon-boot
